WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.430
Acting is a profession that requires a lot
of versatility and willingness to test boundaries.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:09.610
In the act of immersion, sometimes the script
calls for things that the actor himself would

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.720
never even consider, yet they have to play
it naturally.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.660
And sometimes that results in a complete nightmare
for everyone involved.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.410
Here are some movie scenes that actors regret
doing.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.660
A Titanic drawing

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:27.470
Maybe the most memorable scene in Titanic
is the one where Kate Winslet's Rose character

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:32.160
asks Leonardo DiCaprio's Jack to "draw me
like one of your French girls."

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.699
It's a passionate moment showing her character
overcoming the disapproval of her fiancé

00:00:36.699 --> 00:00:40.839
and mother to claim her own agency and embrace
the man she's fallen in love with.

00:00:40.839 --> 00:00:46.589
"As a paying customer, I expect to get what
I want."

00:00:46.589 --> 00:00:51.190
But now obsessive fans try to get Winslet
to sign pictures of herself naked.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.129
And she'd love for that to stop.

00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:54.129
She told Yahoo!

00:00:54.129 --> 00:00:56.489
News, "I don't sign that picture.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.079
It feels very uncomfortable.

00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:00.179
Why would you do that?"

00:01:00.179 --> 00:01:01.969
Why indeed.

00:01:01.969 --> 00:01:03.940
Give that man a shirt

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:08.810
Taylor Lautner played the werewolf character
Jacob in the Twilight series, and his transformations

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:12.280
usually left him shirtless, if not completely
naked.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.439
Fans loved it, but Lautner worries now that
his pecs might overshadow his acting.

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:21.530
He told Ace Showbiz, "If I had to choose,
I would never take my shirt off again in a

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:24.039
movie, but I guess that's not very realistic.

00:01:24.039 --> 00:01:27.240
I certainly won't be asking to do it, though."

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.630
A change of heart

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:35.350
In the 2013 action comedy Kick-Ass 2, Jim
Carrey plays a superhero called Colonel Stars

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:38.350
and Stripes who's gruesomely murdered by supervillains.

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:42.490
A few months after the film was released,
Carrey publicly condemned the level of violence

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:47.270
in the film after experiencing change of heart
in the aftermath of the tragic Sandy Hook

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:51.409
Massacre, which happened shortly after he'd
wrapped up filming his scenes.

00:01:51.409 --> 00:01:57.100
"I did Kick-Ass 2 a month before Sandy Hook
and now in all good conscience I cannot support

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.490
that level of violence....

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:03.210
I am not ashamed of it but recent events have
caused a change in my heart."

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:07.259
While that's a respectable stand to take,
the bosses at Universal Pictures probably

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.080
wished Carey had figured that out before taking
the role.

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.530
Icky drunk stuff

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:17.750
Passengers is a science fiction adventure
starring Jennifer Lawrence and Chris Pratt.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:22.420
Despite the star-power of its cast, it didn't
do very well at the box office, partly due

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:27.390
to backlash against a crucial plot point that
involves a startling disregard for the consent

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:30.130
and personal autonomy of one of the characters.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:34.800
Which wasn't helped by Jennifer Lawrence admitting
that she spent the love scenes too drunk to

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:35.970
remember doing them.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:39.860
She told CNN she had jitters about the shoot
because it was going to be her first time

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:44.390
filming a love scene and also felt guilty about
doing so with Pratt, who's married.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:46.220
"I got really drunk.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.240
But that led to more anxiety because I was
like 'What have I done?

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:50.480
I don't know'…

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.250
And it was gonna be my first time kissing
a married man, and the guilt is the worst

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:57.090
feeling in your stomach."

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:58.650
That leg cross

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:04.690
In Basic Instinct, Sharon Stone plays writer-slash-murderer
Catherine Tramell, who uses her wits and

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:09.470
appeal to easily manipulate the men around
her, especially in the iconic scene where,

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:16.041
by simply uncrossing her legs and *ahem* "flashing
the cash" during a police interrogation, she

00:03:16.041 --> 00:03:18.261
completely reverses the balance of power.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.140
"It's nice."

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:32.780
Which is sort of ironic, because according
to Stone, the scene itself turns out to be

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:36.030
born of manipulation and a violation of consent.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:40.090
Stone claims she was asked by director Paul
Verhoeven to remove her underwear because

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:42.340
the flashes of white were messing up the shot.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:46.410
She was assured there would be no nudity visible
on camera and didn't discover she had been

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:50.560
tricked until she saw the finished film — in
a room full of other people.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:55.210
She responded by slapping Verhoeven, who has
publicly denied Stone's claims, saying, "it's

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:56.690
a lie."

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.180
There's a wall there

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:02.570
In The Phantom Menace, Terence Stamp plays
Chancellor Valorum, who's ushered out in favor

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:07.370
of the secret Sith Lord Palpatine thanks to
a vote of "no confidence" from Queen Amidala,

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:08.820
played by Natalie Portman.

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:12.541
It's about as exciting to watch as an actual
Senate hearing, but it's important to the

00:04:12.541 --> 00:04:15.120
overall plot, or what passes for one.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:19.070
Stamp signed on to the movie for the sole
purpose of getting to act with Natalie Portman.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:23.480
However, when he actually arrived on set,
Portman was nowhere in sight, and Stamp was

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:27.750
directed to aim his dialogue towards a piece
of paper on the wall instead.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:30.500
He told IndieWire, "It was just pretty boring."

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.810
Which, not coincidentally, also sums up the
entire movie.

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:35.810
